    "title": "Antibiotics Confound Breath-Based Respiratory Disease Detection in Calves - Dataset",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.17940806",
    "publication_date": "2025-12-15",
    "description": "<div>\n<p>This dataset supports the paper <em>&ldquo;Antibiotics Confound Breath-Based Respiratory Disease Detection in Calves&rdquo;</em> (PLOS ONE). It contains breath volatile organic compound (VOC) emission rates and clinical metadata collected from calves during two experimental phases:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Tab 1 &ndash; BRD Trial:</strong><br>Emission rates of individual VOCs measured in the breath of healthy and diseased calves using PTR-QiTOF (quadrupole ion guide). Units: &micro;g animal⁻&sup1; h⁻&sup1;, except formaldehyde (mg animal⁻&sup1; h⁻&sup1;) and CO₂ (g animal⁻&sup1; h⁻&sup1;). Metadata includes date/time, animal ID, health status, true disease classification, medications, respiration rate, rectal temperature, clinical scores (nose, eyes, ears, cough, total), and age.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Tab 2 &ndash; Antibiotic Trial:</strong><br>Breath emission rates for four VOCs before and after administration of Alamycin LA300, measured at &ndash;48 h, &ndash;24 h (baseline), and 1 h, 24 h, 48 h, 72 h, and 96 h post-treatment.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>File format:</strong> Excel (.xlsx) with two tabs. Column headers include metadata and VOC formulas (protonated species).<br><strong>Instrument:</strong> Proton Transfer Reaction Time-of-Flight Mass Spectrometer (PTR-QiTOF).</p>\n</div>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
